+# Daily Grind account
+
+Static, responsive account UI. Open through the existing static host. No dependencies or build step are required.
+
+## Passkey integration
+
+The page requests `GET /api/passkeys` using same-origin cookies. If that endpoint is missing (404 or a successful HTML static-host fallback), it displays an explicitly labeled preview account with sample passkeys persisted in localStorage. Sample credentials never invoke authenticator APIs. Network, authentication, and server errors display a retry state instead of falling back to sample data.
+
+Connect an authenticated backend with this contract:
+
+- `GET /api/passkeys` returns `{ rpId, userId, displayName, csrfToken?, credentials }`.
+- Each credential contains `{ id, name, provider?, device?, registeredAt, lastUsedAt?, current? }`. Dates are persisted epoch milliseconds. `device` can be `laptop`, `phone`, or `usb`; unknown devices get a generic key icon. Resolve provider metadata on the backend from stored registration AAGUIDs. `current` must come from trusted session metadata, not browser guessing.
+- `PATCH /api/passkeys/:id` accepts `{ name }` and returns `{ credentials }`, the complete authoritative list after saving.
+- `DELETE /api/passkeys/:id` returns `{ credentials }`, the complete authoritative list after deleting.
+- All endpoints must enforce authentication and credential ownership, reject cross-origin mutations, validate nicknames, and apply the application's CSRF protection. The client sends `X-CSRF-Token` when supplied by GET. Ensure users retain another sign-in method when deleting the last credential, or reject the request according to your recovery policy.
+- `rpId` must match the configured registration RP ID; it is never inferred from the page hostname. `userId` and all credential IDs must be genuine unpadded Base64URL strings.
+
+For real accounts, the client feature-detects `PublicKeyCredential.signalAllAcceptedCredentials` and invokes it on initial load and immediately after a successful deletion. Unsupported browsers and sync failures show manual cleanup guidance without undoing saved account changes. Renaming a passkey only changes its account nickname and never signals a user identity change. Passkey enrollment and profile editing are outside this management screen.
+
+## Checks
+
+`node --check account.js` validates client JavaScript syntax without starting a server. The repository has no build script. Main navigation retains the site's existing route conventions; those destination pages are not included in this static starter.
